A run is claimed, performed and reported
A participant asks the lane what work is available to it, and the lane offers
only runs of steps the participant's identity may take. The participant
claims one, which is a conditional write, and the claim is recorded with its
link in the trail. The participant does the work behind its own firewall and
reports what the step declared; the lane closes the run only if closing is
what that act means. Nothing is ever pushed to the participant, and a claim
held past its deadline is released for somebody else.
